<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/
..\FrameXML\UI.xsd">
	<!-- ========================================================================
	     FriendGroups' OWN contact list for the Classic flavors.

	     Why this frame exists, and why it is not Blizzard's:

	     Rendering into FriendsFrameFriendsScrollFrame means writing fields that
	     Blizzard's own code reads back while the Social window is opening. Those are
	     scrollFrame.buttons and the scroll offset inside FriendsFrame_UpdateFriends,
	     the FriendsFrame_UpdateFriends global itself, FriendsFrame.selectedFriendType,
	     and FriendsTooltip.button. Reading an addon written value taints the rest of
	     that execution, and FriendsFrame_OnShow finishes by calling RaidFrame:Show()
	     when the Raid tab is selected. RaidFrame is protected, because Blizzard_RaidUI
	     parents 40 SecureUnitButtonTemplate raid buttons to it, so in combat that call
	     is refused and the Raid panel never appears. That is CurseForge issue 55, and
	     it costs Classic raid leaders the only way to move people between groups
	     mid fight.

	     So the addon draws into a list of its own and leaves Blizzard's alone. The look
	     is unchanged because the pieces are the same pieces: rows are still
	     FriendsFrameButtonTemplate, the frame is still HybridScrollFrameTemplate, and
	     the bar is still MinimalHybridScrollBarTemplate, which is exactly what
	     Blizzard's own friends list is built from (in FriendsFrame.xml its scroll frame
	     inherits HybridScrollFrameTemplate and its $parentScrollBar inherits
	     MinimalHybridScrollBarTemplate).

	     Loaded ONLY by the Classic tocs. Retail keeps its ScrollBox path untouched.

	     Wiring that comes for free here, and must not be re-implemented in Lua:
	       HybridScrollFrameTemplate's ScrollChild OnLoad sets frame.scrollChild.
	       MinimalHybridScrollBarTemplate carries parentKey="scrollBar", so
	       frame.scrollBar resolves without help, and the template's OnValueChanged is
	       HybridScrollFrame_OnValueChanged.
	       The bar's carets register themselves as frame.scrollUp and frame.scrollDown,
	       via HybridScrollFrameScrollUp_OnLoad reading self:GetParent():GetParent().
	     HybridScrollFrame_CreateButtons needs frame.scrollBar to exist before it runs,
	     which the above guarantees.

	     Parented to FriendsListFrame, the Contacts page itself, so page visibility is
	     inherited: Blizzard shows and hides that frame with the page, and no tab
	     detection is needed. The anchors are the same numbers the addon has always
	     applied when it re-seated Blizzard's list, so the list occupies the identical
	     rectangle. The bar is seated in Lua (FG_SetupOwnClassicList) next to the two
	     cosmetic lines that go with it.

	     Starts hidden: while the own list path is switched off, this frame must not
	     draw over the native one. FG_SetupOwnClassicList shows it.
	     ======================================================================== -->
	<ScrollFrame name="FriendGroupsClassicList" parent="FriendsListFrame" inherits="HybridScrollFrameTemplate" hidden="true">
		<Anchors>
			<Anchor point="TOPLEFT" x="7" y="-115"/>
			<Anchor point="BOTTOMRIGHT" x="-28" y="35"/>
		</Anchors>
		<Layers>
			<!-- The ornate border that frames the scrollbar. Blizzard declares these three
			     on FriendsFrameFriendsScrollFrame itself, so the addon has always drawn
			     them by re-seating that frame; without them the own list would show a bare
			     bar. Copied verbatim: same file, sizes, offsets and tex coords. ElvUI
			     strips them on Blizzard's frame, and the skin adapter does the same here. -->
			<Layer level="BACKGROUND">
				<Texture name="$parentTop" file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\UI-Character-ScrollBar">
					<Size x="29" y="102"/>
					<Anchors>
						<Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativePoint="TOPRIGHT" x="-6" y="5"/>
					</Anchors>
					<TexCoords left="0" right="0.445" top="0" bottom="0.4"/>
				</Texture>
				<Texture name="$parentBottom" file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\UI-Character-ScrollBar">
					<Size x="29" y="106"/>
					<Anchors>
						<Anchor point="BOTTOMLEFT" relativePoint="BOTTOMRIGHT" x="-6" y="-5"/>
					</Anchors>
					<TexCoords left="0.515625" right="0.960625" top="0" bottom="0.4140625"/>
				</Texture>
				<Texture name="$parentMiddle" file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\UI-Character-ScrollBar">
					<Size x="29" y="1"/>
					<Anchors>
						<Anchor point="TOP" relativeTo="$parentTop" relativePoint="BOTTOM"/>
						<Anchor point="BOTTOM" relativeTo="$parentBottom" relativePoint="TOP"/>
					</Anchors>
					<TexCoords left="0" right="0.445" top="0.75" bottom="1.0"/>
				</Texture>
			</Layer>
		</Layers>
		<Frames>
			<Slider name="$parentScrollBar" inherits="MinimalHybridScrollBarTemplate"/>
		</Frames>
	</ScrollFrame>
</Ui>
